damaged_code:
```rust
// Version 1 schema does not know about photo_url
#[derive(serde::Deserialize, serde::Serialize)]
struct PersonV1 {
    user_name: String,
    favorite_number: u64,
}

// Old service instance reads a record containing {"user_name": "Martin", "favorite_number": 1337, "photo_url": "http://..."}
fn update_user_preferences(db_json: &str) -> String {
    let mut p: PersonV1 = serde_json::from_str(db_json).unwrap(); // silently discards photo_url
    p.favorite_number = 42;
    serde_json::to_string(&p).unwrap() // photo_url is permanently deleted upon write-back
}
```

counterexample:
Read-only consumers that neither write back nor forward the original record need not retain every field. Serializers that preserve unknown data and targeted updates that touch only the intended fields avoid this specific loss.
```rust
// Strictly-controlled internal payload that is never written back or forwarded
#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct InternalEvent {
    id: u64,
}
```
